WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.930
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I want to talk about some of the

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:09.370
key moments in the third and final Maze Runner
movie, The Death Cure, as well as how they

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.719
affected its ending, and I'll also reveal
some interesting details, connections and

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:15.600
easter eggs you might have missed in the movie.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.180
If this is your first time on my channel,
I do regular breakdowns of new movies, so

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.340
don't forget to hit the subscribe button and
notification bell to get my videos as soon

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.890
I post them, plus later in the video I'm also
announcing the winner of my latest giveaway.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.981
Quick warning, I will be discussing spoilers
from Maze Runner: The Death Cure, so take

00:00:32.981 --> 00:00:35.940
care if you've not seen the movie yet.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.760
Let's start with the final scene and work
our way back to earlier moments which connect

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.780
to it.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:44.760
Thomas wakes up from his injuries to find
himself in the Safe Haven with Minho and the

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.649
other surviving Immunes.

00:00:46.649 --> 00:00:50.010
And there's an emotional moment for Thomas
when he finds a note inside the necklace that

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.250
Newt gave him.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.079
In the letter, Newt tells his friend that
the thing that scares him most about the virus

00:00:55.079 --> 00:00:56.730
is losing his memory to it.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:01.190
Memory has been an important theme throughout
the Maze Runner films, with the first movie

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:05.841
showing the Gladers having no recollection
of their lives before entering the Maze, and

00:01:05.841 --> 00:01:10.740
note how in this latest film, Teresa wants
to keep her memories of Thomas, despite Ava

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.090
Paige's offer to wipe them away, after all,
as Teresa says, 'if we find a cure that's

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.789
the only way all this was worth it.'

00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:22.689
Ok, back to Newt's letter, he goes on to say
that if he could do everything all over again

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:27.340
he would and he wouldn't change a thing and
he hopes Thomas will feel the same years from

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.340
now.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.619
Newt understands that Thomas has always been
the key to everyone's survival and he tells

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.600
him that "the future is in [Thomas's] hands
now" and that he'll have to find a way to

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.859
do what's right.

00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:42.849
Soon after, when Thomas takes the vaccine
Teresa gave him out of his pocket, Newt's

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:48.179
words turn out to be literally true as Thomas
does indeed hold the secret to saving humanity

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:49.799
in his hands.

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:54.889
Another moment that showcases the trilogy's
key theme of memory is Vince's speech to the

00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:59.299
survivors in the Safe Haven when he reveals
a large memorial stone to honour those who

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:00.299
didn't make it.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.090
If you look carefully you'll spot the names
of characters who died during the series,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:08.209
such as Zart from the first movie, but also
hidden in there are a few crew names like

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:12.510
Wes, a nod to Wes Ball, who directed all three
movies.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.940
This moment also calls to mind the first Maze
Runner movie when the Gladers crossed out

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.310
a name on the maze wall whenever they lost
one of their group.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.630
Thomas carves Teresa's name into the memorial
rock in honour of her sacrifice to save him

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.090
on top of the burning WCKD building.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:31.130
Teresa's death was poignant not only because
of her feelings for Thomas, but also because

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.620
her sacrifice was in keeping with her ultimate
goal to find a vaccine for the Flare virus

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.290
for the whole of humanity, not just the select
few that Janson wanted to help.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:44.110
Although she betrayed the Immunes at the end
of The Scorch Trials, it was only because

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:47.760
she believed in the idea that "WCKD [was]
good" and she always thought the Immunes'

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.620
sacrifice would ultimately save the human
race from devastation.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.480
When Thomas asked her in The Death Cure if
she regretted what she'd done she simply replied

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.480
"Sometimes.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.840
But I did what I thought was right [and] I'd
do it again", a sentiment which is later echoed

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.680
in Newt's letter to Thomas.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.231
As Janson said to Teresa, "What I like about
you is no matter how bleak things get, you

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:12.790
never give up", and in the end, she was the
one who made the breakthrough as she understood

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:17.460
that Brenda's recovery after getting the serum
from Thomas in The Scorch Trials meant something

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.040
different was going on, which is why in this
film she smuggled out Thomas's bloody bandage

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.760
and inspected it in the lab.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.490
Although she found it difficult to see her
friends suffer, in Teresa's mind it was ultimately

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.260
worthwhile for what she saw as the greater
good.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.490
When she and Thomas are on the roof of the
WCKD building, she's aware they're both in

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:40.780
mortal danger and understands that Thomas
is the key to humanity's survival so she gives

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.930
him the serum of his blood that she was carrying
and ensures that he gets on the aircraft first.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.400
With Teresa and Ava Paige dead at the end
of the Death Cure, and the Right Arm's scientist

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.660
Mary killed at the end of The Scorch Trials,
it's not entirely clear who will have the

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:59.330
expertise to replicate the vaccine, but I
guess that somewhere among the survivors there

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.280
may be another scientist who can help.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.890
The other poignant death scene in The Death
Cure was, of course, when Thomas had to kill

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:11.400
Newt after the Flare infection finally turned
Newt into a Crank and he stabbed Thomas in

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.400
the chest.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.590
There was plenty of foreshadowing for Newt's
eventual transformation into a Crank throughout

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.590
the movies.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.400
For example, during Thomas's hallucination
scene in The Scorch Trials, he saw a vision

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.990
of Newt as a Crank.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:27.580
And in The Death Cure, just before Thomas,
Newt and Frypan ventured into the tunnel,

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.699
Newt said "I don't want to come across as
too negative, but if I was a Crank, that's

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:34.009
exactly where I'd be".

00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:37.930
Another thing foreshadowing Newt's death in
this film is a jar containing what appears

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:42.570
to be a dead newt which you can see briefly
in rebel leader Lawrence's room.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.400
Brenda's line to Thomas in the movie, "you
can't save everyone", is also a bit of foreshadowing

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.020
for when Thomas stabs Newt, however, it has
a double-meaning because by the end of the

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:56.219
movie we know that Thomas can save everyone
as his blood is the basis for the ultimate

00:04:56.219 --> 00:04:58.370
vaccine against the Flare virus.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.909
There's also a nice parallel between Newt
giving his necklace to Thomas once he realises

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:07.229
he's unlikely to survive and Chuck who gave
Thomas his wooden carving as he died in the

00:05:07.229 --> 00:05:09.280
first Maze Runner film.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.039
And when Newt explained to Thomas that WCKD
must have put him into the maze "so they could

00:05:13.039 --> 00:05:17.159
tell the difference between immunes like you
and people like me", it's a reference to Newt's

00:05:17.159 --> 00:05:22.469
backstory in the books where Newt had a sister
who was an Immune abducted by WICKED.

00:05:22.469 --> 00:05:26.949
In the books, WICKED decided to take Newt
with them as well to use him as a control

00:05:26.949 --> 00:05:31.479
subject in their trials to see how Immunes
performed compared to ordinary people like

00:05:31.479 --> 00:05:32.479
him.

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:36.780
One new character we meet in The Death Cure
is Lawrence, the rebel leader Gally's working

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.919
for outside the Last City.

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:43.340
When we meet him for the first time he has
a curious interest in roses, despite the loss

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:45.509
of his nose and much of his face to the Flare
virus.

00:05:45.509 --> 00:05:50.349
This version of Lawrence is a clever reference
that book fans will recognise as he's partially

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:55.020
based on the "Rose took my nose" Crank that
Thomas encountered in The Scorch Trials book

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.970
but who never made it into the second Maze
Runner movie.

